%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec4ba6a512adabf4b8a74985cb2f4d14, type: 3}
  m_Name: VladDay1Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptedDialogue
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    npcLine: So. You are the replacement.
    animationTrigger: 
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: You look exactly like the last one. Same uniform, same nervous eyes.
    animationTrigger: TalkCocky
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: Same face that says I have no idea what I agreed to. Good. That means
      you are normal. For now.
    animationTrigger: TalkDismissing
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: My name is Vladimir Syrnikov. You will call me Vlad.
    animationTrigger: TalkBigCocky
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: Outside this booth, you will not say that name. This is not vanity.
      It is simply how things are.
    animationTrigger: TalkDismissing
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: Tell me. What do you know about what comes through this gate?
    animationTrigger: TalkPoint
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: Civilians, migrants, documented travelers.
      npcResponse: Mm. The paperwork version. Cute. You are going to have a very
        interesting first week.
      animationTrigger: TalkDismissing
    - playerChoiceText: Whatever the briefing didn't cover, I assume.
      npcResponse: Ha! I like that. Pessimism and self-awareness. You may survive
        after all. Do not get comfortable.
      animationTrigger: ShortLaugh
  - type: 0
    npcLine: Most of what you will see is boring. Papers, stamps, faces, send them
      through.
    animationTrigger: TalkShrug
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: You will wish for something to happen. Do not. The boring days are the
      gift.
    animationTrigger: TalkDismissing
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: "When something wrong walks through that window \u2014 and it will \u2014
      what is your instinct?"
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: Follow the rulebook. Document everything.
      npcResponse: The rulebook. Yes. Good friend, the rulebook. Until it has never
        seen what you are looking at. Then it is useless paper.
      animationTrigger: TalkSarcasticNod
    - playerChoiceText: Trust my gut. Make a call.
      npcResponse: "Your gut. Good. Your gut will be smarter than you, most of the
        time. The times it is not \u2014 those are the times that end careers. Or
        worse."
      animationTrigger: TalkCocky
  - type: 0
    npcLine: There are things coming through this gate that your training did not
      cover.
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: "When you encounter one \u2014 do not panic. Do your job. The paperwork
      will lie. The face might lie."
    animationTrigger: TalkPoint
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: But something about them will feel wrong. Trust that. It has kept me
      alive for fifteen years.
    animationTrigger: Talk1
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: You have questions. I can see them. Keep them for now.
    animationTrigger: TalkShrug
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: "Do your job, stay sharp, and if you last the week \u2014 maybe I answer
      some of them."
    animationTrigger: 
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: Try not to disappoint me, Officer. It would be genuinely inconvenient.
    animationTrigger: TalkBigLaugh
    choices: []
